# How the framework's roll-at-grant-time reward kinds read on a chip.
# The file name is the key PREFIX: an entry here resolves as ziggfreedcommon.loot.<key>.
#
# These are the labels the shipped Lootable / Droplist / Effect kind files point their NameKey at:
# none of the three can promise a specific item ahead of time, so each reads as one generic line (a
# Lootable only when its table is set to PlainBundle; otherwise it reads as its table's own name).
# A reward that writes its own NameKey outranks these; a mod shipping the same key in its own lang
# file outranks this library's copy.

reward.lootable = Loot Bundle
reward.droplist = Loot Drop
reward.effect = Temporary Effect

# What hovering a Lootable reward lists (unless its table sets ListContents false). Each line ends with the
# reward's own line ("x3 Lantern Bomb"), after one space: what always comes reads alone, a chance leads
# with its percent ({0}, at most one decimal), and what something else decides leads with "Sometimes:".
# Two closing lines may follow, in this order: preview.more when the table holds something the list
# cannot name, and preview.hidden when the table keeps a roll out of the list on purpose (HideInPreview).
preview.chance = {0, number}%:
preview.sometimes = Sometimes:
preview.more = Plus a little more.
preview.hidden = And a few more rare finds.
